 "news": {
  "date": "2026-09-10",
  "asof": "2026-09-11 09:24 UTC",
  "headline": "Palantir is three-quarters of a per cent from its stop \u2014 and CPI prints at 08:30",
  "standfirst": "Citigroup cut Palantir to Market Perform on valuation and the stock closed 165.86, 0.75% above its stop, on volume 54% below average. That is a position at its line rather than near it, and an ordinary session resolves it. Around it the tape deteriorated for a fourth straight day: the S&P fell 0.58% to 7,591.70 and closed below its 50-day for the first time in this sequence, WTI settled at $102.48 with Saudi production reported at its lowest since 1990, the ten-year rose 11bp to 4.94% and the thirty-year to its highest since June 2007, and net gamma deepened again to \u2212$44.19B. One thing went right: AAPL rose 3.56% after Deepwater doubled its iPhone Duo revenue estimate, turning the position green. Heat 4.04R against 3.0R.",
  "themes": [],
  "ondeck": "August CPI lands today, Friday 11 September at 08:30 ET, and is the regime's tightest gate; the Bank of Japan meets next week with a hike 97% priced; the FOMC meets 15\u201316 September; triple witching is 18 September. Tomorrow's brief covers the CPI session and carries the weekly.",
  "note": null
